    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nTimeless Luxury on the Shores of Lough CorribDNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents are proud to present Kitts Bay, a truly exceptional lakeside residence set on the shores of Lough Corrib in one of the most private and picturesque settings in the west of Ireland.Located just 7 km from the thriving village of Oughterard, this impressive home enjoys uninterrupted views across the lake and surrounding countryside. The setting is peaceful and sheltered, offering a rare sense of privacy while remaining within easy reach of local amenities and Galway City.Set on approximately 1.43 acres of mature landscaped grounds, Kitts Bay comprises a substantial main residence extending to approximately 622 sq.m. together with a detached boathouse extending to approximately 44 sq.m. The residence has been carefully designed to take full advantage of its unique waterfront position, with bright, spacious rooms and large windows capturing stunning lake views.Approached via a long private driveway, the sense of arrival is immediate, with established planting and generous grounds creating a feeling of space and seclusion. The gardens are beautifully maintained and include expansive lawn areas, mature trees and shrubs, as well as an orchard and a number of outdoor seating areas designed to enjoy the surroundings at all times of the day.Internally, the accommodation is both generous and thoughtfully arranged, offering an excellent balance between everyday living and entertaining. The main reception areas are bright and welcoming, with large windows perfectly framing the ever-changing views across Lough Corrib.The lounge is a particularly impressive space, ideally positioned to take in the lake views and suited to both quiet evenings and entertaining guests. The adjoining dining room offers a warm and comfortable setting for family gatherings while maintaining a strong connection to the landscape outside.At the heart of the home lies a spacious open plan kitchen and family dining area, fitted with quality units, granite worktops and integrated appliances. This space opens directly onto the outdoor decking, creating a seamless connection between indoor and outdoor living and making it ideal for both everyday family life and larger gatherings.A separate family entrance leads to a thoughtfully designed family wing comprising a comfortable family room, private office, family WC and utility areas, providing a practical yet highly functional space for everyday living.The bedroom accommodation is impressive throughout. The master suite provides a private and spacious retreat, complete with two dressing areas and well-finished bathroom facilities. Five further bedrooms, all of which are ensuite, offer excellent accommodation for family and guests alike.Upstairs, a large landing area currently in use as a gym and games room provides further flexibility and enjoys elevated views across the lake, with access to additional deck areas that fully embrace the stunning surroundings.One of the most exceptional features of Kitts Bay is its direct access to Lough Corrib, with a private pier and sheltered cove offering a rare opportunity for boating, fishing and lakeside living at its finest. The detached boathouse, while currently unfinished, presents excellent potential for conversion into guest accommodation or a leisure space, subject to the necessary consents.The outdoor areas are a defining feature of the property, offering the perfect setting for morning coffee by the water, summer dining or simply enjoying the tranquillity of this remarkable location. A combination of raised decking, paved patio areas and mature planting ensures the grounds can be enjoyed throughout the year.Additional features include underfloor heating at ground floor level, solar panels for hot water, modern connectivity, and an exceptional standard of finish throughout, including high-quality carpets by Dixon Carpet Company, formerly V'Soske Joyce.The surrounding area is renowned for its natural beauty and local attractions, with nearby amenities including the historic Currarevagh Country House, Corrib Lodge offering Italian cuisine, the scenic Hill of Doon viewpoint with views across Lough Corrib, together with Derroura Wood and the Western Way walking trail, both highly regarded for walking, cycling and exploring the unspoilt Connemara landscape.Oughterard offers a wide selection of amenities including schools, shops, cafes and restaurants, while Galway City is within comfortable commuting distance, making this an ideal location for both a permanent residence and a luxurious retreat.Lough Corrib, famed for its vast waters, hidden inlets and hundreds of islands, is regarded as one of Ireland's most spectacular lakes and is internationally renowned for its fishing, boating and unspoilt beauty. The surrounding landscape of rugged countryside, winding shoreline and ever-changing lake views creates a unique atmosphere seldom found today and further enhances the appeal of this exceptional lakeside home.Opportunities to acquire a property of this calibre in such a private and sought after lakeside setting are extremely rare. Viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the quality, scale and unique lifestyle this exceptional home has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall / Guest Hall - \nA bright and welcoming entrance hall providing access to the main living areas and guest accommodation.\n\nGuest Suite - \nA spacious guest suite complete with bedroom and sitting area, ensuite bathroom, wet room style shower and private sauna.\n\nGuest WC - \nConveniently located, serving the main living and entertaining areas.\n\nLounge - \nA large reception room enjoying excellent natural light and views across Lough Corrib, ideal for both relaxing and entertaining.\n\nDining Room - \nA well-positioned dining area overlooking the lake, providing a warm and inviting setting for family meals.\n\nKitchen / Family Dining Area - \nA spacious open plan kitchen and dining area fitted with quality units, granite worktops and integrated appliances. A separate larder provides excellent additional storage, while direct access to the outdoor decking creates an ideal space for indoor and outdoor living.\n\nFamily Hall / Rear Entrance - \nPractical everyday entrance accessed from the courtyard, linking to the main living areas.\n\nPrivate Office - \nA dedicated home office with built-in storage, offering a quiet workspace separate from the main living areas.\n\nCloakroom - \nLocated off the family hall providing additional storage.\n\nFamily WC - \nA practical facility serving the family living areas.\n\nFamily Room - \nA bright and comfortable living space with wraparound windows and access to the deck.\n\nMaster Bedroom Suite - \nA substantial and private suite comprising a large bedroom, two dressing rooms and two bathrooms, offering a high level of comfort and space.\n\nGarage and Plant Area - \nAttached garage with additional storage and adjoining plant room housing the boiler and services.\n\nOutdoor Decking - \nLarge ground floor deck accessed from the main living areas, ideal for outdoor dining and entertaining.\n\nLanding / Gym and Games Area - \nA large open landing currently used as a gym and games space, offering excellent flexibility and natural light.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nA spacious double bedroom with ensuite shower room.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nA well-proportioned bedroom with ensuite shower room.\n\nBedroom 5 - \nA generous bedroom with ensuite shower room.\n\nBedroom 6 - \nA bright double bedroom with ensuite shower room.\n\nLaundry Room - \nSeparate laundry room with storage and access to an external drying area.\n\nUpper Deck Areas - \nTwo elevated deck areas accessed from the first floor, offering excellent views across Lough Corrib and the surrounding landscape.\n\nBoathouse and Pier - \nDetached boathouse located at the water's edge with covered pier structure and direct lake access. The boathouse includes a ground floor and mezzanine level and offers excellent potential for further use, subject to the necessary consents.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Landmark waterfront residence on the shores of Lough Corrib</li><li> Main residence extending to approx. 622 sq.m.</li><li> Detached boathouse extending to approx. 44 sq.m.</li><li> Approx. 1.43 acres of mature private grounds</li><li> Private pier and sheltered cove</li><li> Direct water access for boating and fishing</li><li> Detached boathouse with conversion potential</li><li> Extensive sun decking and entertaining areas</li><li> Landscaped gardens with orchard and established planting</li><li> Elegant six-bedroom residence</li><li> Ground floor underfloor heating</li><li> Solar hot water heating system</li><li> Attached garage with extensive storage</li><li> Just 34 km from Galway</li><li> Approx. 126 km from Shannon Airport</li><li> Approx. 114 km from Ireland West Airport Knock</li><li> Rare opportunity to acquire a premier waterfront home</ul>"
      },
